d(42)\n","torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(42)\n","\n","# 3. Set random seeds for NumPy and random modules\n","np.random.seed(42)\n","random.seed(42)\n","\n","# 4. Configure PyTorch deterministic behaviors\n","torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\n","torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\n","\n","print(\"Random seeds initialized successfully and deterministic backend configured!\")"],"execution_count":2,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["WARNING: CUDA GPU is not available. Running on CPU.\n","Random seeds initialized successfully and deterministic backend configured!\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"9a15d3f9"},"source":["# Task\n","Implement the complete pipeline for instruction-tuning GPT-2 (124M) on the WebNLG 2017 dataset to translate structured triples into natural language sentences. Your code must cover:\n","1. **Environment Setup**: Install `tiktoken`, `sacrebleu`, `gradio`, and other required libraries.\n","2. **GPU & Seed Setup**: Verify GPU availability and set reproducible seeds.\n","3. **Dataset Acquisition & Parsing**: Download, extract, and parse the XML-based WebNLG 2017 dataset from official or reliable sources.\n","4. **Data Preprocessing**: Format the parsed triples into Alpaca-style instruction-input-response formats.\n","5. **Tokenization & Datasets**: Create a custom PyTorch Dataset and a collate function using `tiktoken` to prepare masked inputs (prompt masking with -100) for causal language modeling.\n","6. **Custom GPT-2 Architecture**: Implement the GPT-2 (124M) architecture from scratch using pure PyTorch.\n","7. **Pretrained Weights Loading**: Download the official OpenAI GPT-2 124M weights and load them parameter-by-parameter into your custom architecture.\n","8. **Baseline Evaluation**: Generate text with the pre-trained weights before fine-tuning.\n","9. **Fine-Tuning Loop**: Fine-tune the model on the WebNLG dataset using the Cross-Entropy loss on non-masked tokens.\n","10. **Quantitative Evaluation**: Plot training/validation loss curves and calculate BLEU scores using `sacrebleu` before and after fine-tuning.\n","11. **Qualitative Evaluation**: Inspect 15 example outputs for factual correctness against original triples to check for hallucinations or omissions.\n","12. **Gradio Application**: Build a Gradio interface allowing users to input raw triples and receive the generated natural language sentence from your fine-tuned model."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"a965c7c5"},"source":["## Section 1: Environment Setup & Library Installation\n","\n","### Subtask:\n","Install required dependencies and import Python libraries for the project.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"cab33e0c"},"source":["## Section 2: GPU Verification & Seed Initialization\n","\n","### Subtask:\n","Verify GPU availability and initialize random seeds across libraries to ensure reproducibility.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"865c19c4"},"source":["## Section 3: WebNLG 2017 Dataset Acquisition & Parsing\n","\n","### Subtask:\n","Download, extract, and parse the XML-based WebNLG 2017 dataset to extract structured triples and natural language targets.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"4aa13694"},"source":["**Reasoning**:\n","We will download, extract, and parse the WebNLG 2017 dataset XML files into structured Python formats (train, dev/val, test splits) using urllib, zipfile, and xml.etree.ElementTree.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"40973f82","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1793542625351,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":719,"user":{"displayName":"Sahana","userId":"04785986170074206494"}},"outputId":"694b7841-a69f-4557-90e3-dc85c413ac44"},"source":["import os\n","import shutil\n","import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n","import pandas as pd\n","\n","clone_dir = \"webnlg_repo\"\n","extract_dir = \"webnlg_extracted\"\n","\n","# 1. Clone the WebNLG repository using git clone for robustness\n","if not os.path.exists(clone_dir):\n","    print(\"Cloning WebNLG dataset repository...\")\n","    os.system(f\"git clone https://github.com/shimorina/webnlg.git {clone_dir}\")\n","    print(\"Cloning completed!\")\n","\n","# Search directory for XML files\n","def find_xml_files(directory):\n","    xml_files = []\n","    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(directory):\n","        for file in files:\n","            if file.endswith(\".xml\") and not file.startswith(\".\"):\n","                xml_files.append(os.path.join(root, file))\n","    return xml_files\n","\n","# 2. Parsing Function for WebNLG XML structure\n","def parse_webnlg_xml(file_paths):\n","    data = []\n","    for file_path in file_paths:\n","        try:\n","            tree = ET.parse(file_path)\n","            root = tree.getroot()\n","            for entry in root.findall(\".//entry\"):\n","                category = entry.attrib.get('category', 'unknown')\n","                # Extract Triples\n","                triples = []\n","                triples_elem = entry.find('modifiedtripleset')\n","                if triples_elem is None:\n","                    triples_elem = entry.find('originaltripleset')\n","                if triples_elem is not None:\n","                    for mtriples in triples_elem.findall('otriple') + triples_elem.findall('mtriple'):\n","                        if mtriples.text:\n","                            triples.append(mtriples.text.strip())\n","\n","                # Extract Lexicalizations\n","                lexicalizations = []\n","                for lex in entry.findall('lex'):\n","                    if lex.text:\n","                        lexicalizations.append(lex.text.strip())\n","\n","                if triples and lexicalizations:\n","                    data.append({\n","                        'category': category,\n","                        'triples': triples,\n","                        'lexicalizations': lexicalizations\n","                    })\n","        except Exception as e:\n","            print(f\"Error parsing {file_path}: {e}\")\n","    return data\n","\n","# Locate files under webnlg_challenge_2017 subfolder in the cloned repository\n","all_xml_files = find_xml_files(clone_dir)\n","\n","train_files = [f for f in all_xml_files if \"train\" in f.lower()]\n","dev_files = [f for f in all_xml_files if \"dev\" in f.lower() or \"val\" in f.lower()]\n","test_files = [f for f in all_xml_files if \"test\" in f.lower()]\n","\n","# Parse splits\n","train_data = parse_webnlg_xml(train_files)\n","dev_data = parse_webnlg_xml(dev_files)\n","test_data = parse_webnlg_xml(test_files)\n","\n","print(f\"Parsed Train Set: {len(train_data)} entries\")\n","print(f\"Parsed Dev Set: {len(dev_data)} entries\")\n","print(f\"Parsed Test Set: {len(test_data)} entries\")\n","\n","# Show a quick sample\n","if train_data:\n","    print(\"\\nSample parsed entry:\")\n","    print(train_data[0])\n"],"execution_count":10,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Cloning WebNLG dataset repository...\n","Cloning completed!\n","Parsed Train Set: 0 entries\n","Parsed Dev Set: 0 entries\n","Parsed Test Set: 0 entries\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"3be28300"},"source":["**Reasoning**:\n","The previous code block successfully cloned the repo, but returned 0 parsed entries. This is because git clone cloned the repo into 'webnlg_repo', but the XML files might be inside compressed folders (like zip files inside the cloned repo) or the path search did not match the subdirectories correctly. Let's inspect the files in 'webnlg_repo' to understand its structure and locate the XML files or extract any zip archives inside it.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"a9966f43","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1793542632723,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":9,"user":{"displayName":"Sahana","userId":"04785986170074206494"}},"outputId":"bc42f3b2-5bd